Some of the prominent aspects that may be taken into consideration to draw an inference regarding the mental state of the accused are as under:-
(i) the number of injuries;
(ii) the nature of injuries received by the victim;
Jaishankar Sharma vs State Of Rajasthan on 4 September, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/81733467/
11 (iii) the kind of weapon used by the accused for inflicting injury;
(iv) the part of body which the accused chosen to inflict the injury;
(v) the other surrounding circumstances like time and place of incident whether it was crime place belonged to the accused or it belonged to the victim or a random public place;
(vi) previous animosity between the accused and victim which must be of such a degree which would indicate itself strong reason or motive of the accused so as to show the intent to cause death of the victim.
